<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n66442" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεσό-κοιλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hollow, low-lying</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					10.10.7
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Agathem.
				5.20
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>hollow in the middle</i>, of a stalk, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.11
			</span></i>; of the heart, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Anat.</u>
				32
			</span></i>; <i>grooved</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξύλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					1.83
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ μ.,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεσόδμη</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Am.</u>
				6
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
